n't need to call start_exam? The instruction says \"call start_exam when ready\" but the tools list only show_transformed_input. There is no start_exam tool. Maybe we just provide final answer after 4 pairs? Or maybe the environment automatically enters exam? The user says \"then call start_exam when ready.\" But there is no start_exam function in the tool list. Possibly we just call show_transformed_input 4 times and then final response. We cannot call start_exam because not provided. We should just do the tool calls. Perhaps the harness interprets multiple calls as adding pairs and then we finish. We'll do 4 calls in parallel? They are independent. We can call all 4 in one block.\n\nLet's ensure inputs are rectangular 3x3. Yes.\n\nLet's write the calls.",
